  derive from `final_model.dart` via per-feature partial-dependence curves
  (replacing the old hand-tuned Normal-CDF gauges); fixed the hourly model
  call-site mis-wire so `nuptialHourlyPercentageModel` passes the model's real
  9-feature order `[lat, lon, hour, temp, wind, humid, press, dewPoint,
  daysSinceSpring]`. `flutter analyze` stays at 0 errors; `nuptials_test.dart`,
  `hourly_test.dart`, `model_test.dart` all pass.

## Guardrails
- Keep first-page load fast: do not re-introduce `await` on
  `initializeService()` or the notification permission before `runApp()`.
- Do not hand-edit the generated `models/*.dart` score trees.
- Prefer `git -C` and verify with `flutter analyze` before claiming done.
- `flutter pub upgrade` has been observed to HANG for many minutes
  (stuck resolving git deps). If it does not finish quickly, kill the
  `dart.exe` processes and use `flutter pub get` instead to reconcile
  `pubspec.lock`. Note: `flutter pub get` may print a non-fatal
  Windows error about deleting `windows/flutter/ephemeral/.plugin_symlinks`
  — that is a desktop-build dir permission quirk and is safe to ignore.
- README.md was expanded (2026-07-18) with features, data flow,
  setup/.env template, and project structure — keep it in sync if you
  add user-facing features or change required API keys.
- Keep the model call-site feature orders in `nuptials.dart` in sync with the
  training notebooks (`lib/models/*.ipynb`). The hourly model uses 9 features
  (no rain/cloud); the daily uses 10. A mismatched order silently produces
  wrong predictions — the hourly call site was mis-wired until 2026-07-26.

## Resumable work — model retrain + training findings (2026-07-26)
A model-improvement effort is in progress (NOT yet committed to production).
Resume from the state below. Do NOT overwrite `lib/models/final_model.dart`
or `assets/final_model.json` without explicit user approval.

### Live training data source
- ArangoDB at `https://api.bitbot.com.au:8530` (TLS only), db
  `nuptialFlight`, collection `flights` (212,504 docs). DB credentials are the
  ones already committed in `lib/models/autosklearn_classification.ipynb`
  (user `notebook` + the password in that notebook) — not duplicated here.
  Connect with python-arango:
  `ArangoClient(hosts='https://api.bitbot.com.au:8530'); db=client.db('nuptialFlight', username='notebook', password=<from notebook>)`.
- ⚠️ Security: the DB contains a defaced collection
  `u have been pwned bro contact me at: policenational@cyberfear.com`.
  Rotate the `notebook` DB user's password and audit for unauthorised changes.

### Tooling constraints (this environment)
- Shell commands have a **30 s per-call cap**; **background processes are
  reaped between calls**. Run inline and keep each call <30 s; for long
  fetches use resumable chunked scripts (state file + dedup-on-read).
- **Project only needed fields in AQL** (`RETURN {field…}` not `RETURN f`)
  — ~30× faster transfers (60 k docs in ~2 s).
- Python 3.9.13 + sklearn/pandas/numpy/arango/m2cgen/sklite installed.
  matplotlib/seaborn/nbconvert/xgboost are NOT installed (not needed).

### Cached state (in `%TEMP%` = `C:\Users\Brad\AppData\Local\Temp`)
- `flights_cache.csv` — all 212,504 flights; cols
  `target,lat,lon,dayOfYear,dt,day,windSpeed,rain0,humid,cloud,press,dewPoint,rain1,rain2,key`
  (dedup-safe on `key`).
- `df.pkl` — feature-engineered DataFrame (212,504 rows; 10,127 positives =
  4.77%). Added cols: `dss` (daysSinceSpring = `(dayOfYear-243)%365`, NH
  subtract 184), `hemisphere`, `sin_doy`, `cos_doy`, `dew_dep=day-dewPoint`,
  `lat_r`, `lon_r`.
- `baseline_model.pkl` — RF reproducing production params (64 trees,
  `max_features=10`, `min_samples_split=3`, `ccp_alpha=0.0008`).
  **DEGENERATE:** every tree pruned to a single leaf (`node_count=1`,
  importances sum 0.0, **AUC 0.500, AP 0.048**). ⇒ production
  `ccp_alpha=0.0008` collapses the forest under 4.77% class imbalance.
- `improved_model.pkl` — RF(150, `max_features='sqrt'`,
  `min_samples_leaf=5`, `max_depth=14`, `class_weight='balanced_subsample'`,
  no ccp_alpha). Features (`imp_cols`, 15):
  `[lat, lon, hemisphere, sin_doy, cos_doy, day, windSpeed, rain0, humid,
  cloud, press, dewPoint, dew_dep, rain1, rain2]`.
  **Result: acc_te 0.895, f1 0.164, AUC 0.663, AP 0.110** (vs baseline
  AUC 0.500). Top importances: lat .12, lon .117, day .101, dewPoint .088,
  windSpeed .087, sin_doy .081, dew_dep .073.
- `features.json` = `{"base":[...10...], "imp":[...15...]}`.
- `holdout.pkl` — 2000 test samples (`{'X':df,'y':series}`) for parity.
- Scripts in TEMP: `fetch_chunk.py` (resumable projected fetch,
  `FETCH_BATCH` env), `prep.py`, `train_base.py`, `diag_imp.py`.

